    <h2>Marking with the Unified Grader</h2>
    <p>How to open the grader, read a submission, give a grade and feedback, and release it to students.</p>
</header>

{{! ----- Quick start ----- }}
<section id="quickstart">
<h3>Mark your first submission</h3>

<ol class="local-unifiedgrader-help-steps">
    <li><strong>Open the grader.</strong> On the activity page, choose <strong>Unified Grader</strong>
        in the activity's navigation (on an assignment it comes after <em>Submissions</em> and
        <em>Advanced grading</em>), or press the <strong>Grade</strong> button.</li>
    <li><strong>Pick a student.</strong> Use the previous and next arrows beside the counter
        (<em>3 / 24</em>), or open the <a href="#grader-tour">student list</a> to search, filter and sort.</li>
    <li><strong>Read the work</strong> on the left. Documents open with
        <a href="#feature-annotations">annotation tools</a>. Forum posts, quiz attempts and
        recordings show as they are.</li>
    <li><strong>Grade and comment</strong> on the right: the grade or the rubric, then
        <strong>Overall Feedback</strong>. Press <strong>Save feedback</strong>. The header shows
        <em>All changes saved</em>.</li>
    <li><strong>Post the grade</strong> when you are ready for the student to see it, with the
        <a href="#feature-post-grades">post-grades control</a> in the header.</li>
</ol>

<figure class="local-unifiedgrader-help-shot">
    <a href="{{img.entry_points}}" data-action="help-zoom">
        <img src="{{img.entry_points}}" width="1300" height="748" loading="lazy"
             alt="An assignment page for a teacher. A Unified Grader item sits in the activity navigation after Assignment, Settings, Submissions and Advanced grading, and a Grade button sits above the grading summary.">
    </a>
    <figcaption>Two ways in from an assignment: the <strong>Unified Grader</strong> item in the
    activity navigation and the <strong>Grade</strong> button.</figcaption>
</figure>

<div class="local-unifiedgrader-help-note local-unifiedgrader-help-note-req">
    <p><strong>You need permission to grade.</strong> The grader opens only for users who hold
    <code>local/unifiedgrader:grade</code> in the activity: editing teachers and managers by default.
    A non-editing teacher sees no Unified Grader item until an administrator grants it.
    See <a href="#admin-capabilities">Capabilities</a>.</p>
</div>

<p>The <i class="fa fa-question-circle" aria-hidden="true"></i> button in the grader opens this page
at the section for the activity you are marking.</p>
</section>

{{! ----- The grader screen ----- }}
<section id="grader-tour">
<h3>The grader screen</h3>

<h4>Header</h4>
<p>From left to right:</p>
<ul>
    <li><strong>Course and activity</strong> links, with <strong>View all submissions</strong>.</li>
    <li><strong>The student</strong>: name, submission date and a status badge. Click the name for a
        small profile card with <strong>View full profile</strong> and <strong>Send mail</strong>.</li>
    <li><strong>Status badge menu</strong>: actions for this student's submission (see below).</li>
    <li><strong>Submission comments</strong> icon: <a href="#feature-notes">messages with the student</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>Save status</strong>, for example <em>All changes saved</em>.</li>
    <li><strong>Post-grades control</strong>: <a href="#feature-post-grades">show or hide grades</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>Friction feedback</strong>: <a href="#feature-friction">Site default, On for this activity or Off for this activity</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>Layout buttons</strong>: <em>Dual file view</em> (only when a submission has more than
        one source), <em>Split view</em>, <em>Preview only</em>, <em>Grading only</em>.</li>
    <li><strong>Previous / next</strong> with a counter, the <strong>student list</strong> button and the help button.</li>
</ul>

<div class="local-unifiedgrader-help-shots">
    <figure class="local-unifiedgrader-help-shot">
        <a href="{{img.status_menu}}" data-action="help-zoom">
            <img src="{{img.status_menu}}" width="760" height="241" loading="lazy"
                 alt="The status badge, reading Submitted, with its menu open: Revert to draft, Remove submission, Dates and extensions.">
        </a>
        <figcaption>The status badge menu on a submitted assignment.</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <figure class="local-unifiedgrader-help-shot">
        <a href="{{img.profile_popout}}" data-action="help-zoom">
            <img src="{{img.profile_popout}}" width="1200" height="682" loading="lazy"
                 alt="A small card under the student's name with their picture and two buttons: View full profile and Send mail.">
        </a>
        <figcaption>The profile card opens from the student's name.</figcaption>
    </figure>
</div>

<h4>What the status badge menu offers</h4>
<div class="local-unifiedgrader-help-table">
<table class="table-reboot">
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Activity and status</th><th scope="col">Actions</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr><th scope="row">Assignment, submitted</th><td>Revert to draft, Remove submission, Dates &amp; extensions</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Assignment, draft</th><td>Edit submission, Prevent submission changes, Submit for grading, Remove submission, Dates &amp; extensions. A locked draft offers <em>Allow submission changes</em> instead.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Quiz, forum</th><td>Dates &amp; extensions only</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Rated forum, BigBlueButton</th><td>No menu</td></tr>
    </tbody>
</table>
</div>
<p>When a student already has an override or an extension, the menu also offers
<strong>Clear all overrides</strong>. Each action asks for confirmation.</p>

<h4>Student list</h4>
<p>The list button opens every participant you may see.</p>
<ul>
    <li><strong>Search</strong> by name.</li>
    <li><strong>Filter</strong>: All participants, Submitted, Not submitted, Graded, Ungraded, Late.</li>
    <li><strong>Sort</strong>: Full name, Submission date, Status.</li>
    <li>Each row shows a short status badge (<em>Sub</em>, <em>Grd</em>, <em>Dft</em>) and an eye:
        open when that student's grade is posted, struck through when it is hidden.</li>
    <li>On a proctored quiz, each row also carries a coloured
        <a href="#feature-proctoring">review-priority marker</a>.</li>
    <li>In a course with groups, a <a href="#feature-groups">group selector</a> sits above the list.</li>
</ul>

<figure class="local-unifiedgrader-help-shot local-unifiedgrader-help-shot-narrow">
    <a href="{{img.navigator}}" data-action="help-zoom">
        <img src="{{img.navigator}}" width="1200" height="750" loading="lazy"
             alt="The student list open under the header: a search box, a filter set to All participants, a sort set to Submission date, and four students, each with an eye icon and a status badge.">
    </a>
    <figcaption>The student list: search, filter, sort, a posted or hidden eye, and a status badge per student.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>

